2d4dcc76e26888ea7f31d14553266f594f","event_uuid":"254bc95b-c12e-4fa4-80ad-72c94b7cec32","position":{"commit_sha":"a12d506b383b50a0d190aac088a4aff75de82b04","position":"1793902580345474873-254bc95b-c12e-4fa4-80ad-72c94b7cec32"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-308_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"a85e3cd3-9e61-4f25-9de4-cd740e853b4d","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause confirmed read-only over SSM (2026-11-04 03:00 PST): the live container rebar-mcp-4496e9acd2a9-8092 mounts only gerrit_mcp_tickets, gerrit_mcp_code, /var/lib/rebar and two secrets; /var/gerrit/site/.rebar (where StorePaths.log puts compact-worker.log) is on the writable layer. The container logs via journald tag=rebar-mcp, and journalctl -t rebar-mcp still holds lines from 2026-10-30, i.e. it survives releases. Fix follows that precedent: compact.worker_log=stderr (REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG) set in compose and mcp_run_new. New tests failed before the fix (4 failed, 3 passed) and pass after; the touched files plus config/infra drift tests: 331 passed; make lint and make typecheck clean. Pushed as Gerrit 3300.","timestamp":1793793199123150001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3300 merged as 1a23adaf04e5db1548ac8e0d0e3650414dc96339 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1 on run 41824490749). Read-only SSM, 2026-11-04 04:25 PST: mcp-deployed-sha = 1a23adaf04e; container rebar-mcp-1a23adaf04e5-8092 carried REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr. At 04:36 PST a later deploy (fe6c2100292) had replaced it: the container is gone from docker ps -a, yet journalctl CONTAINER_NAME=rebar-mcp-1a23adaf04e5-8092 still returns its 69 lines through its 04:30 PST shutdown. AC3 NOT yet met: no compaction sweep ran in that container (0 'rebar._commands.compact' lines in journalctl -t rebar-mcp across all releases), so no sweep log has yet been shown to survive a deploy. Remaining check: after the first MCP close that fires a sweep and the following deploy, run journalctl -t rebar-mcp | grep rebar._commands.compact on the host. Ticket left in_progress; AC1/AC2 boxes left unticked until the close so the plan attestation stays current. Discovered: exemplary-silty-tuatara (trigger lock and sweep stamp are also on the writable layer).","timestamp":1793795827995202001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Follow-up per operator ruling (a bug fix may not add a config key): Gerrit 3332 removes compact.worker_log / REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG entirely and decides the sweep log at the call site. The MCP transition_ticket tool pins the private library kwarg _sweep_log=\"stderr\" (same pattern as _creation_channel=\"mcp\"); rebar.transition -> transition_compute -> close_ticket -> maybe_compact -> _spawn_detached_sweep carries it. The CLI and direct library callers keep the store's .rebar/logs/compact-worker.log. No new mechanism of any kind (check_mechanism_delta --check exits 0, stale=0, so no baseline change). Removed: schema field + section validator + both markers, compose and mcp_run_new env, docs/config.md entry, regenerated config-reference/env-vars/config_surface golden. Tests first: MCP close spawns a sweep with stderr fd 2 and no log file; CLI close's sweep stderr is the store log file; key absent from the config surface. Before: 2 failed, 1 passed (CLI path was already the default). After: pass. Blue-green test now proves the tool pin -> journald driver/tag on the replacement container chain. make verify passed (20844 + 202 integration passed).","timestamp":1793902162906479001}],"created_at":1793725895836000001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6f125f81-e28a-4911-961b-891dd50b1162","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"467d-e068-ee33-4bad"},{"link_uuid":"4feaa9d1-5e39-4ac3-a158-3627ecf05837","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8d2c-2805-1ebf-4d2e"},{"link_uuid":"254bc95b-c12e-4fa4-80ad-72c94b7cec32","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"66b9-860e-38d7-4a29"}],"description":"## Problem\nThe compaction sweep's log, /var/gerrit/site/.rebar/logs/compact-worker.log inside the rebar-mcp container, is not on a volume. autodeploy.sh replaces the container on every src/rebar change (2-minute timer), so the log is discarded at each deploy. The Nov 1 PST sweep's log was lost this way, which left breezelike-travelsick-moray without per-phase production timings; Gerrit 3269 (f1fe7c6f587) added those timing lines, but they survive only until the next deploy.\n\n## Root cause\n- `_spawn_detached_sweep` (src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:122-147) opens `StorePaths(tracker).log(\"logs/compact-worker.log\")` and hands it to the detached child as stderr. `StorePaths.log` (src/rebar/_store/paths.py:105) puts it in the `.rebar/` directory BESIDE the tracker, i.e. `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar/` for the deployed tracker `/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`.\n- The mcp service mounts only `gerrit_mcp_tickets` (the tracker itself), `gerrit_mcp_code`, `/var/lib/rebar` and two secrets (infra/compose/docker-compose.yml:262-273; autodeploy.sh `mcp_run_new` mirrors them). `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` is on the container's writable layer, so `docker rm` of the retired release deletes it.\n- Confirmed read-only over SSM on 2026-11-04 against the live container (`rebar-mcp-4496e9acd2a9-8092`): mounts are exactly those five; `/var/gerrit/site/.rebar` does not exist yet in the hour-old container; the container's PID 1 is `rebar-mcp` with fd 1/2 on Docker pipes; LogConfig is `journald tag=rebar-mcp`; `/var/log/journal` is persistent with an explicit `SystemMaxUse` cap (infra/scripts/journald-cap.sh), and `journalctl -t rebar-mcp` still returns lines from 2026-10-30, i.e. from earlier releases.\n\n## Approach\nFollow the existing precedent rather than add a volume: the MCP server's own log already survives every blue-green deploy because the mcp service logs to journald under one tag (docker-compose.yml:281-286, mirrored as `--log-driver journald --log-opt tag=rebar-mcp` in autodeploy.sh, guarded by `test_docker_run_matches_compose_mcp_logging`). The journal is already capped and retained by journald-cap.sh, so this needs no new volume and adds no new retention policy.\n\n1. Add a config key `compact.worker_log` to `CompactConfig` (src/rebar/_config_schema.py, beside `trigger`) with choices `file` (default, unchanged behaviour) and `stderr`, parsed with `_as_choice` in src/rebar/_config_sections.py's `compact` section like `compact.trigger`. It is settable through the canonical env override `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG`, exactly as the deploy already sets `REBAR_SYNC_PUSH`. Marker: `# mechanism-ok: config_key compact.worker_log — 4f4d-9a7a-3b2d-4b13`.\n2. `maybe_compact` already reads `cfg = compose_config(repo_root).compact`; pass `cfg.worker_log` to `_spawn_detached_sweep`. With `stderr`, the child is handed the spawning process's own fd 2 instead of the file, and no log file is opened. In the container the spawner is the rebar-mcp server (MCP writes run in server threads, src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:110), whose fd 2 is the Docker pipe, so the sweep's records reach `journalctl -t rebar-mcp` with the `WARNING rebar._commands.compact: compaction fold timing: ...` prefix from `install_stderr_handler`.\n3. Set `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG: \"stderr\"` in the compose mcp service and `-e REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr` in `mcp_run_new`; the existing compose/docker-run parity test then guards both.\n4. Docs: name the read command in docs/mcp-client-setup.md Troubleshooting; describe the key in docs/config.md and the worker-log sentence in docs/concurrency.md; regenerate docs/config-reference.md, docs/env-vars.md and tests/golden/config_surface.json with their generators.\n\n`file` stays the default: local and CI stderr is a terminal or a pipe a caller waits on for EOF, which a detached child must not hold open.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_config_schema.py, src/rebar/_config_sections.py — new `compact.worker_log` key.\n- src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py — choose the child's stderr from the key.\n- infra/compose/docker-compose.yml, infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh — set the key to `stderr` for the MCP container.\n- tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py, tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py — tests.\n- docs/mcp-client-setup.md, docs/config.md, docs/concurrency.md, docs/config-reference.md, docs/env-vars.md, tests/golden/config_surface.json — docs and generated artifacts.\nOut of scope: shipping logs off the box (fab-dismal-haddock); the snapshot-GC worker's own log.\n\n## Testing\nFailing tests first, in the existing files, no autouse fixtures:\n- tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py: with `worker_log=\"stderr\"`, the fake Popen receives stderr fd 2 and no `compact-worker.log` is created; with the default `file`, the child's stderr is the opened log file at `_trigger_log_path` (regression guard); `compact.worker_log = \"bogus\"` in config is rejected by the parser; `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr` in the environment yields `compose_config(...).compact.worker_log == \"stderr\"`.\n- tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py: the compose mcp service sets `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG` to `stderr`, and the docker run line carries `-e REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr` (the existing parity test also covers it).\n- Run the touched test files, `make lint` and `make typecheck` with the worktree .venv/bin first on PATH.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] The compact-worker log persists across a blue-green MCP deploy (on a mounted volume or forwarded to the journal like rebar-mcp's own log), with a test or config check that guards the location. Verified by the tests above passing, and by the compose file and `mcp_run_new` both setting `REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr`.\n- [x] docs/mcp-client-setup.md troubleshooting (or the MCP runbook) names where to read it: `journalctl -t rebar-mcp | grep rebar._commands.compact`.\n- [x] [non-codebase] After the next deploy, the log from the previous container is still readable.\n  provenance: environment=production host i-00880b2c7f13527c5 journald; principal=operator session via SSM AWS-RunShellScript under the instance role; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — 2026-11-04 20:2x PST: journalctl -t rebar-mcp holds compaction fold timing lines from the 13:04-13:11 PST sweep (container rebar-mcp-7c3cb5e9a4f9-8093) and the 17:09-17:17 PST sweep (rebar-mcp-81f77e005686-8093); both containers had been replaced by later deploys and the current one is rebar-mcp-38c42c7e70e9-8092, and /var/gerrit/site/.rebar holds no logs/ directory.\n  provenance: production-equivalent / live-call","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"add compact.worker_log"},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_sections.py","reason":"parse compact.worker_log"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py","reason":"route the detached sweep stderr per compact.worker_log"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"set REBAR_COMPACT_WORKER_LOG=stderr on the mcp service"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"mirror the env in mcp_run_new"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py","reason":"worker log routing tests"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"guard the deployed log location"},{"path":"docs/mcp-client-setup.md","reason":"name where to read the sweep log"},{"path":"docs/config.md","reason":"document the key"}